# Fix: existing subscribers never get enrolled in the skills email course

Repo: `/Users/joel/Code/badass-courses/ai-hero`, app `apps/ai-hero`. Work on a
branch off `main` named `fix/skills-enrollment-existing-subscribers`. Write
code and tests. Do NOT commit, push, or merge. Steering reviews and ships.

## The bug (diagnosed, confirmed in prod)

Existing active Kit subscribers who open `/skills/subscribe` see the
"subscribed" state: a static "Check your inbox for the first lesson." box.
Nothing enrolls them. No form-add, no `skills-newsletter/subscribed` event.
The page comment claims the hourly reconciler guarantees path entry. It does
not, for two reasons:

1. They never POST, so they never join Kit form 9376133, and the reconciler
   only scans form members.
2. `buildSignupGapPreview` in
   `src/lib/subscriber-marketing/signup-gap-recovery.ts` (~line 185) filters
   `inWindow` on the subscriber ACCOUNT `createdAt >= 2026-07-15`. The Kit
   fetch in `signup-confirmation-reconciler.server.ts` already filters by form
   `added_after=2026-07-15` at the API level. The in-memory re-check on
   account age wrongly drops anyone whose Kit account predates 2026-07-15,
   which is most of the list. The record already carries `addedAt`; the window
   check must use `addedAt`, not `createdAt`.
3. Same function (~line 219): any subscriber with an existing `contact` row or
   `providerIdentity` is skipped. "Known contact" is not "entered the course".
   Replace this with a check for an actual course entry (see
   `DrizzleCaptureMarketingRepository` and how
   `enterSkillsNewsletterSubscriber` records entries; find the table that
   records path entry and query that instead).

## Required changes

### 1. Page: `src/app/(content)/skills/subscribe/page.tsx`

When the resolved subscriber is active, actually enroll them instead of only
reassuring. Requirements:

- Add them to Kit form 9376133 (`emailListProvider.subscribeToList`, same as
  `tagSubscriberAsSkills` in
  `src/app/(content)/skills/_components/skills-newsletter-actions.ts`) and
  send the `skills-newsletter/subscribed` event with
  `source: 'skills-subscribe-page-recognized'`.
- Use a DETERMINISTIC Inngest event id per subscriber, for example
  `skills-page-entry:9376133:<kitSubscriberId>`, so repeat page views can
  never double-enroll. Entry is also idempotent downstream
  (`idempotentNoop`), this is belt and braces.
- Do not block page render on the Kit/Inngest calls failing; log failures
  with `log.error` and still render the reassurance UI.
- Keep the reassurance copy. No third click. A recognized active subscriber
  landing on this page IS the intent signal (Joel's confirmation-equals-
  enrollment ruling, 2026-07-21).

### 2. Reconciler window: `signup-gap-recovery.ts`

- `buildSignupGapPreview` window filter uses `addedAt` (form join time), not
  `createdAt` (account age). The type already threads `addedAt` through from
  `signup-confirmation-reconciler.server.ts`; if the preview type lacks it,
  add it.
- HARD GUARDRAIL: the standing ~25k historical form backlog (form joins
  BEFORE 2026-07-15) must stay excluded. The API-level
  `added_after=2026-07-15` param plus the corrected `addedAt` window keeps
  that true. Never widen the window start. Add a test asserting a subscriber
  with `addedAt` before 2026-07-15 is NOT a candidate even with a fresh
  account.

### 3. Identity skip: `signup-gap-recovery.ts` + reconciler server

- Replace the `hasContact || hasProviderIdentity` skip with an "already has a
  course path entry" check. A past purchaser or newsletter contact who newly
  joined the form after 2026-07-15 MUST become a candidate.
- Keep the synthetic-address exclusion and the 200-per-run limit exactly as
  they are. The limit is the flood brake.

## Tests

Extend the existing test files for these modules (they exist, follow their
patterns). Must cover at least:

- old account + form `addedAt` after 2026-07-15 + no entry → candidate
- any account + form `addedAt` before 2026-07-15 → never a candidate
- contact row exists but no course entry → candidate
- course entry exists → skipped
- page: active subscriber render sends form-add + event with deterministic
  id; inactive subscriber gets the form, no event
- page: Kit/Inngest failure logs and still renders

Run the relevant test suites plus typecheck and report results honestly. If
you cannot make a test pass, say so; do not weaken assertions.

## Constraints

- No commits, no pushes, no shitrat. Leave the branch dirty for review.
- Do not touch the Kit API `added_after` param, the 200 limit, or anything
  under `value-path-*` beyond what the entry-check requires.
- No em dashes in any copy. No customer emails in code, comments, or tests.
- When done, print `DONE FIX` plus a file list and test results summary.
